                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "Oh, I see.\r\nI was using the default leader key `\\`, but I didn't have this set anywhere in my `init.lua` file or in my plugins, so the `mini.basics` was changing it.\r\nNow that I explicitly set this in `init.lua`, the problem was solved.\r\nThanks for your help. ",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Oh, I see.<br>\nI was using the default leader key <code class=\"notranslate\">\\</code>, but I didn't have this set anywhere in my <code class=\"notranslate\">init.lua</code> file or in my plugins, so the <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.basics</code> was changing it.<br>\nNow that I explicitly set this in <code class=\"notranslate\">init.lua</code>, the problem was solved.<br>\nThanks for your help.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Oh, I see.\nI was using the default leader key \\, but I didn't have this set anywhere in my init.lua file or in my plugins, so the mini.basics was changing it.\nNow that I explicitly set this in init.lua, the problem was solved.\nThanks for your help.",
